{"symbol":"TSC1","resolved":{"input":"TSC1","symbol":"TSC1","ncbi_gene_id":"7248","name":"TSC complex subunit 1","location":"9q34.13","aliases":["LAM","TSC"],"uniprot":"Q92574","uniprot_reviewed":true},"function":[{"text":"TSC1 function (UniProt Q92574, UniProt evidence code ECO:0000269): Non-catalytic component of the TSC-TBC complex, a multiprotein complex that acts as a negative regulator of the canonical mTORC1 complex, an evolutionarily conserved central nutrient sensor that stimulates anabolic reactions and macromolecule biosynthesis to promote cellular biomass generation and growth. The TSC-TBC complex acts as a GTPase-activating protein (GAP) for the small GTPase RHEB, a direct activator of the protein kinase activity of mTORC1. In absence of nutrients, the TSC-TBC complex inhibits mTORC1, thereby preventing phosphorylation of ribosomal protein S6 kinase (RPS6KB1 and RPS6KB2) and EIF4EBP1 (4E-BP1) by the mTORC1 signaling. The TSC-TBC complex is inactivated in ...","evidence":"experimentally validated","code":"EXP","citations":[{"source":"UniProt","id":"Q92574","url":"https://www.uniprot.org/uniprotkb/Q92574/entry","title":"TSC1: Hamartin"},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:10585443","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/10585443/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12172553","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12172553/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12271141","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12271141/","title":""},{"source":"PubMed","id":"PMID:12906785","url":"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12906785/","title":""}]}],"go":[{"text":"TSC1 GO biological process annotations: activation of GTPase activity, cell-matrix adhesion, cellular response to starvation, negative regulation of ATP-dependent activity, negative regulation of cell population proliferation, negative regulation of TOR signaling, negative regulation of TORC1 signaling, positive regulation of focal adhesion assembly, protein stabilization, regulation of cell-matrix adhesi